SUMMARY:Full Frontal Comedy Is Back In The Attic!
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington
DESCRIPTION:Full Frontal Comedy is Indiana University’s longest-running c
 omedy group\, bringing laughs to Bloomington and beyond since 1994. FFC is 
 a student-led IU club.\n\nEvery Full Frontal show kicks off with a prewritt
 en sketch before launching into a high-energy lineup of short-form improv g
 ames followed by a long form section called a montage. No two shows are the
  same\; everything is based on audience suggestions.\n\nFull Frontal’s cu
 rrent performing members are Kuran Patel\, Katherine Stalmah\, Marshall Zag
 otta\, Natalie Orban\, Calvin Barron\, Zach Gates\, Dylan Ross\, Brenzlee J
 ohnson\, Kaelyn Wallin\, Carter Kinnett\, and Oscar Bernfield. Hailing from
  across the country and studying everything from Marketing to Piano Perform
 ance\, FFC brings together a motley crew of students united by a timeless c
 ollege tradition: making each other laugh and hoping everyone else joins in
 .\n\nFull Frontal Comedy performs every other Friday in the State Room East
  in the IMU. Follow [handle removed] on Instagram for upcoming shows and mo
 re.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/full-frontal-com
 edy-is-back-in-the-attic/
